-- title:
--   Noise commutes with sign probabilities
-- statement:
--   On the Boolean cube $\{0,1\}^n$, $\mathbb Eg=2^{-n}\sum_xg(x)$ is the uniform average and $T_u$ is the noise operator with kernel $K_u(x,y)=\prod_i\frac{1\pm u}2$, with the sign $+$ when $x_i=y_i$. The sign law with mean $v$ gives the bit $b$ probability $p_v(b)=\frac{1+v}2$ if $b$ is true and $\frac{1-v}2$ otherwise.
--
--   For every soft function $g$, correlation $u$, bit $b$ and point $x$,
--   $$
--   T_u\bigl(p_{g(\cdot)}(b)\bigr)(x)=p_{T_ug(x)}(b).
--   $$
--
--   So the output bit of a soft channel followed by noise has the sign law of the noised function.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/InformationTheory/BooleanNoise/FiniteDistribution.lean#L25-L40

